      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "The handbook states and proves the (G)/(L)/(O)/(R) equivalence only for a probability law on the standard Borel product (body 113-120). It proves this through the cycle recursive => global => local => ordered => recursive (annex 170-242), so ordered-to-global passes through regular conditional kernels. The cited source Theorem 2.44 (cited at body line 7; source pp. 64-66) is stated for an arbitrary semigraphoid independence model. Its proofs of (L)=>(G), by terminal-vertex induction, and of (O)=>(L), by induction via (2.29), use only the semigraphoid axioms, and Corollary 2.45 gives order-invariance of (O). That abstract-semigraphoid variant is neither stated nor proved on the route; a handbook-wide search finds semigraphoid treatment only for probabilistic operations. Needed: state the (G)/(L)/(O) equivalence for any semigraphoid independence model and prove (O)=>(L) and (L)=>(G) from the semigraphoid axioms alone, or cite where that variant is treated.",
